sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila mauritiana Turing wavelength at 1.6 µm (Pass 2, assimilated ocellus) — MorphoEval overall 89.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the free branch (FFT wavelength 1.562 µm versus 1.637 µm; analytical k_max at 1.629 µm) and locks the 12-frame, 640×480 GIF onto the nudged ocellus. Official CV similarity of that last frame is 93.9 (pass 1 free-field CV was 87.5). Pearson r against the specimen-derived target is 0.9997, RMSE is 0.0070, KS is 0.0337. Foreground fraction is 0.413 versus 0.378 on the illustration; coherency is 0.790 versus 0.785. Equal diffusion is stable and decays. D_v/D_u from 7.5 to 13.5 lengthens λ monotonically. Successor D. melanogaster at 1.22× inhibitor range selects 1.701 µm. A 38.4 µm compact-lobe window holds 23.6 detail ridges and 0.41 of a kikkawai 93.41 µm cellular wave. Age 0 Ma. Weighted overall on rubric.yaml is 89.4. Nanopub signing was not available (no ~/.nanopub/profile.yml). Overall 89.4/100 (faithfulness 89.1, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/gif, 2846729 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 b8adad8b9810f34a569f79b9c45b8440a40c678556299fbc727095d61fdb54fe (sha256 b8adad8b9810f34a569f79b9c45b8440a40c678556299fbc727095d61fdb54fe), spec_fingerprint bd0352c8a7daa2adc4a69dc6bf727442d96608f6e6279c8f820e0a58060ad4e4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: bd0352c8a7daa2adc4a69dc6bf727442d96608f6e6279c8f820e0a58060ad4e4; artifact_sha256: b8adad8b9810f34a569f79b9c45b8440a40c678556299fbc727095d61fdb54fe; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_mauritiana.jpg=0c64a140705a3c42..., datasets/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_mauritiana_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=837cc650677e6049...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-mauritiana-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse farther than the activator. | Murray 1981 dependence of intrinsic wavelength on the diffusivity ratio. | Kondo & Miura 2010 as the review frame for stripes, spots, and related RD patterns. | Glassford et al. 2015: posterior-lobe novelty in the melanogaster subgroup, including mauritiana.; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-specific Schnakenberg calibration: D_u = 2.40e-14 m²/s, D_v/D_u = 9.875, γ set so k_max = 2π/1.637 µm. | Nudge κ(T − u) assimilates the gallery ocellus. The GIF endpoint is that field, upsampled and colorized. | Successor wavelength is k_max recomputed at D_v × 1.22, not a parameter copied from a melanogaster script. | Predecessor comparison is the 93.41 µm kikkawai cellular wavelength versus this 1.637 µm detail wavelength.; transfer_boundary: 1.637 µm is the assigned detail scale (tier 3_subcellular_um), not a length reported by Gompel or Glassford. | The 38.4 µm window is a reconstructed comparison length for mode counting.; does_not_claim: That an unforced Schnakenberg system draws the gallery spiral. The free branch is a spot field at 1.562 µm. | That the gallery illustration is a micrograph of the mauritiana genital arch. | That pixel Pearson r is an unforced prediction. It is the assimilated branch. | A second independent assessor.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.1]: Single builder-assessor. No second provider scored the rubric.",
            "remediation needed: An independent second assessor has not scored this slot.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the gallery ocellus illustration with a species-specific micrograph of the mauritiana genital arch if one becomes available; Commons had none on 2026-10-27.",
            "remediation needed: The unforced branch remains a spot field at 1.562 µm. Pixel correlation belongs to the nudged branch only." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.894"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

